de created by Wylte\n- New ball image and scratches based on VPW's tables\n- Updated PWM on flashers GI and Inserts, added 3D inserts and converted 1 pair of inserts to work with Flupper Domes\n- Updated apron primitive from VPW's The Simpsons Party\n- Small color and light corrections on the playfield texture\n- Added insert decals from the Emperor Mod\n- Added Instruction Cards provided by Carny Priest\n- New GI\n- Updated Rubber Dampeners (v.2.2)\n- Removed a lot of timers to improve performance (v.2.2)\n- VPW Tweak Menu added to replace the old VPW Options UI (v.2.2)\n- Slingshots are solenoid driven, based on VPW's Spider-Man Classic (v.2.2)\n- Added a second flasher dome inside the safehouse and edited the safehouse primitive (v.2.2)\n- Added more options for reflections (v.2.3)\n- Added a third VR room for Mixed Reality (v.2.3)\n- Created a new Jet plastic primitive, used and edited texture from Future Pinball version made by NitroNimbus (v.2.3)\n- Added shadows texture from FSS version made by Morttis (v.2.3)\n- Added new flipperbats from VPW's AC/DC, changed flippersizes and triggers to match and edited the texture (v.2.3)\n\nDaRdog:\n- Added VR Mega Room\n- New cab art and apron art\n- Big uprez in the playfield using AI (Updated v.2.3.1 by RKP)\n\nDGrimmReaper:\n- Added key, new flipperbuttons, startbutton, screws on the siderails and plunger and animated them.\n- Re-aligned cabinet to prevent the apron being cut off (v.2.3)\n\nThemer (v.2.2):\n- Inverted VPM switch assignments 43 and 45 (both at the visibleLock and the 'Suitcase lock buttons'). Those switches were inverted\n- New code for the SolSniper sub and the entire sniper section\n- New code for the SolSafehouse sub and the entire safehouse section\n- New VPM solenoid assignment 21 for the suitcase motor\n- Removed the SuitRot property from the solSuitcase sub as this property is removed entirly\n- New MotorSuitcase sub and new code for the entire suitcase section\n\nLoadedWeapon (v.2.2):\n- Created a custom sideblades primitive to fit on Legends Cabinets and provided a secondary ini file for the POV to match\n\nGravy (v.2.3):\n- Edited the old custom jet made by 32assassin\n\nSpecial thanks to everybody involved during development and testing :H3RBSKIx, geradg, BountyBob, Smaug, MikeDASpike, DarthVito, passion4pins, Apophis, m.carter78, somatik, guus_8005, Studlygoorite, Sinizin\n\nShoutout to:\n\n- Carny Priest for the instruction cards he gave us!\n- passion4pins for the backdrop he created for desktop players\n- freneticamnesic, Rascal, luvthatapex, Javier15, unclewilly, oooPLAYER1ooo, rom, zedonius, dark, ASOT, gtxjoe, ICPjuggla, 85vett, arngrim, 32assassin, DGrimmReaper, Emperor, NitroNimbus & Morttis for their work on\nprevious versions\n\nIf I didn't mention anybody else in this development cycle I am unaware of this and just know that I still think you are awesome and also want to say you rock!\nAnd basically everybody from VPW I didn't mention just for having me as part of the family, you all absolutely rock!⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀"
    }
  ],
